.TH SINDOOK-CONTACTS 1 "2026-08-31" "sindook 0.11.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sindook-contacts \- save and use named recipient public keys and groups
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sindook contacts
[\fBlist\fP [\fB\-json\fP] | \fBadd\fP [\fB\-f\fP] \fINAME\fP
\fIPUBLIC_KEY_OR_FILE\fP | \fBshow\fP \fINAME\fP | \fBremove\fP \fINAME\fP]
.br
.B sindook contacts group
[\fBadd\fP [\fB\-f\fP] \fINAME\fP \fIMEMBER\fP... |
\fBlist\fP [\fB\-json\fP] | \fBshow\fP \fINAME\fP |
\fBadd\-member\fP \fINAME\fP \fIMEMBER\fP... |
\fBremove\-member\fP \fINAME\fP \fIMEMBER\fP... |
\fBremove\fP \fINAME\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Saves shareable recipient public keys under portable,
case-insensitive names. Use a saved contact anywhere a recipient is
accepted, for example \fB\-r @alice\fP. A group is a named recipient
list: \fB\-r @team\fP seals to every member, deduplicated, in sorted
member order. Groups list saved contacts only (no nesting), and names
are shared between contacts and groups, so one name is never both. The
configuration file contains public keys, group member lists, and an
optional default identity path only; it never contains private keys or
passphrases. The fingerprint shown by \fBlist\fP is the first 16 bytes
of SHA\-256 over the decoded public key, lowercase hex with a
\fBsha256:\fP prefix: a 128\-bit collision space used to recognize a
contact at a glance, not to authenticate it.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B list
list saved contacts as \fB@name\fP plus a short \fBsha256:\fP key
fingerprint; \fBshow\fP prints the full public key (with \fB\-json\fP:
one JSON array of contacts with full public keys)
.TP
\fBadd\fP [\fB\-f\fP] \fINAME\fP \fIPUBLIC_KEY_OR_FILE\fP
save a public key under \fINAME\fP; \fB\-f\fP replaces an existing
contact
.TP
\fBshow\fP \fINAME\fP
print one saved public key
.TP
\fBremove\fP \fINAME\fP
delete a saved contact; refused while any group lists the contact
.TP
.B group add
[\fB\-f\fP] \fINAME\fP \fIMEMBER\fP...
create a group of saved contacts; \fB\-f\fP replaces an existing group
.TP
.B group list
list saved groups with their members (with \fB\-json\fP: one JSON array
of groups with name, members, and added_at)
.TP
.B group show
\fINAME\fP
print the members of a group, one name per line
.TP
.B group add\-member
\fINAME\fP \fIMEMBER\fP...
add saved contacts to a group
.TP
.B group remove\-member
\fINAME\fP \fIMEMBER\fP...
remove members from a group; a group keeps at least one member
.TP
.B group remove
\fINAME\fP
delete a group; the contacts themselves are kept
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sindook contacts add alice alice.key.pub
sindook contacts add bob bob.key.pub
sindook contacts list
sindook seal -r @alice report.pdf
sindook contacts group add team alice bob
sindook seal -r @team report.pdf
sindook contacts group add-member team carol
sindook contacts group remove-member team bob
sindook contacts group remove team
sindook contacts remove alice
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sindook (1),
.BR sindook-config (1),
.BR sindook-paths (1),
.BR sindook-seal (1)
